The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/core-deep/coredeep-02-rng-seed-propagation.md`.

**Summary of findings:**

| Severity | # | Description |
|----------|---|-------------|
| **Critical** | 1 | Dwelling RNG is dead state — stored but never consumed during simulation. `self.rng` is only used for checkpoint I/O, never sampled in `run_timestep`. |
| **High** | 2 | No hierarchical RNG chain from dwelling to actors/equipment. EV driver and event loads independently derive seeds from names/config rather than from the dwelling RNG. |
| **High** | 3 | No end-to-end reproducibility test for the full simulation with same config seed. |
| **Medium** | 4 | `rng.rs` seed construction uses raw byte-copy instead of a cryptographic KDF. |
| **Medium** | 5 | EV driver seed hash uses a weak polynomial fold (non-cryptographic, poor distribution). |
| **Low** | 6 | Checkpoint RNG serialization is structurally correct (just needs the RNG to actually be used). |
| **Low** | 7 | Fleet mode correctly avoids cloning RNGs via per-dwelling `bldg_id`, but relies on `bldg_id` uniqueness without a defensive assertion. |
